# GitFlow Workflow

Follow [Atlassian GitFlow](https://www.atlassian.com/git/tutorials/comparing-workflows/gitflow-workflow). In this repo, production is `master` and integration is `develop`.

## Branch roles

| Branch | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `master` | Official release history; tag releases here |
| `develop` | Integration branch for upcoming release |
| `feat/*` | New work; parent is always `develop` |
| `release/*` | Release prep (bug fixes, docs only); parent is `develop` |
| `hotfix/*` | Production patches; parent is `master` only |

Never merge features directly into `master`. Never branch features from `master`.

## Agent workflow

### New feature

1. Branch from latest `develop`: `git checkout develop && git pull && git checkout -b feat/<short-name>`
2. Commit on the feature branch
3. Open PR targeting `develop` (not `master`)
4. After merge, delete the feature branch

### Release

1. Branch from `develop`: `git checkout -b release/<version>`
2. Only release fixes (no new features)
3. Merge into `master`, tag version on `master`
4. Merge back into `develop` (captures release fixes)
5. Delete `release/<version>`

### Hotfix

1. Branch from `master`: `git checkout master && git pull && git checkout -b hotfix/<short-name>`
2. Fix, then merge into both `master` and `develop`
3. Tag updated version on `master`
4. Delete the hotfix branch

## Rules

- Before starting work, confirm current branch matches the task type (feature → `develop`, hotfix → `master`)
- Prefer PRs for merges into `develop`, `master`, and `release/*`
- Do not push to `master` or `develop` directly unless the user explicitly asks
- Do not create commits on `develop` or `master` for feature work; use a `feat/*` branch
